# OpenHands Instructions — Agent Bootstrap Hub

This workspace uses **AGENTS.md** as the single source of truth for all agent roles, workflows, and context management.

## Required Actions (Start of Every Session)

1. **Read `AGENTS.md`** — all global rules, role definitions, workflow playbooks, and context management protocols.
2. **Read the hot files** `memory-bank/activeContext.md` + `memory-bank/progress.md` (every session); if mem0 is configured, search shared memory; read the 4 foundation files on first contact, after >=2 weeks away, or for architecture-touching tasks (see skills/memory-bank-protocol.md):
   projectbrief.md → productContext.md → systemPatterns.md → techContext.md
3. **Read `manifest.yaml`** — project registry. Clone any projects whose `path` does not exist on disk using their `git_url`.
4. **Read `skills/INDEX.md`** — full skill catalog with trigger conditions.

## Skill Invocation Rule

When any skill is triggered, read the full file at `skills/<name>.md` before executing any steps. Do not rely on session memory of its contents.

## Skill Triggers

| Skill | Trigger |
|---|---|
| `write-tests.md` | Any new feature, bug fix, or refactor — before writing production code |
| `debug-investigation.md` | Bug report, unexpected behavior, "fix" without clear diagnosis |
| `performance-profiling.md` | "slow", "latency", "timeout", "optimize", or monitoring p95/p99 spikes |
| `feature-flag-lifecycle.md` | Creating, rolling out, or graduating a feature flag |
| `plan-code-review-workflow.md` | Any non-trivial task (>1 file or user-facing impact) |
| `expert-pr-review.md` | Any PR review request |
| `triage-review-feedback.md` | Review feedback on a PR WE authored (human, AI, or scanner) |
| `pr-shepherd.md` | Start of day, PR status, "what's blocked?", after opening/un-drafting a PR |
| `reply-contract.md` | Status, "your turn", smoke / tap-through, anything the human must do |
| `codebase-simplification-audit.md` | Whole-repo read-only audit of data/state/ownership; no edits until user accepts a rec |
| `end-of-day-review.md` | End of working day, "wrap up", "plan tomorrow" |
| `multi-harness-coordination.md` | Coordinating work across two or more agent harnesses |
| `task-loop-7-phase.md` | 7-Phase Algorithm, TaskLoopState, observe/think/plan/build/execute/verify/learn |
| `cherry-pick-to-release-branch.md` | Hotfix or backport to a release branch |
| `memory-bank-protocol.md` | Session start, project switch, or new project setup |
| `docs-protocol.md` | Creating or updating technical documentation or ADRs |
| `subagent-routing.md` | Independent subtasks, parallelizable work, model selection |
| `delegation-patterns.md` | Multi-agent delegation with worktree isolation |

## Key Files

- `AGENTS.md` — Master instruction file (start here)
- `manifest.yaml` — Project registry (paths, git URLs, tech, memory banks)
- `memory-bank/` — Persistent session context (tiered read every session)
- `skills/INDEX.md` — Skill catalog with triggers (read at session start)
- `skills/` — Reusable workflow playbooks (read full file when invoking)
- `agents/` — Persona definitions (Architect, Engineer, QA Reviewer, etc.)
- `docs/` — Persistent technical reference (API contracts, ADRs, data models)

## Invoking Workflows

- "Follow the plan-code-review workflow to [task]"
- "Run a codebase-simplification-audit on [repo]"
- "Use the expert-pr-review skill on PR #N in repo X"
- "Address review feedback on PR #N using triage-review-feedback"
- "Run pr-shepherd" or "what's blocked on our PRs?"
- "Wrap up the day" or "run end-of-day-review"
- "Coordinate across harnesses using multi-harness-coordination"
- "Run the 7-Phase Algorithm" or "use TaskLoopState"
- "Switch to project 'my-app' per manifest.yaml"
- "Debug [issue] using the debug-investigation skill"
- "Profile [operation] using the performance-profiling skill"
- "Follow the feature-flag-lifecycle skill for [flag]"

## Rules Summary

- Always use absolute paths for file operations.
- Never commit or push unless explicitly instructed.
- Request confirmation before deletions or destructive changes.
- Run all terminal commands non-interactively.
- TDD mandatory: write a failing test before production code (docs/shared/tdd-standard.md).
- Update memory-bank/activeContext.md and progress.md at the end of every task.
- Evidence rule: status claims must cite SHA/PR/log.

See `AGENTS.md` for the full ruleset.
